scala-2.13 for Debian
=====================

This is the Scala 2.13 series, packaged next to the scala package (2.12).
Both can be installed together: the jars carry versioned names
(scala-library-2.13.18.jar, scala-library-2.13.jar), the commands are
also available as scalac-2.13, scala-2.13, scaladoc-2.13, fsc-2.13 and
scalap-2.13, and /usr/bin/scala and friends are update-alternatives,
pointing at the newest series installed.

Two-pass self-host build (no sbt)
---------------------------------

debian/build-driver.sh compiles the Scala 2.13 module layers (library,
reflect, compiler, interactive, repl, repl-frontend, scaladoc, scalap)
straight with a STARR scalac, then assembles the jars. debian/rules runs it
twice:

  pass 1: STARR = scala-2.13 from the archive -> jars in debian/buildout1
  pass 2: STARR = the pass-1 jars             -> jars in debian/buildout2

Only the pass-2 jars are installed. The source package contains no
prebuilt jar or class file.

Stage-0 bootstrap seed (provenance and reproducibility)
-------------------------------------------------------

Scala 2.13 can only be compiled by a Scala 2.13 compiler, so the very first
build needs a seed, as for every self-hosting compiler in Debian. It is the
only non-source input, it is used once, and it is never part of the source
package or of any binary package.

The seed is exactly the STARR that upstream itself pins for this release,
in versions.properties at the packaged tag:

  starr.version=2.13.17

i.e. upstream's own published 2.13.17 jars:

  https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/org/scala-lang/scala-library/2.13.17/scala-library-2.13.17.jar
    sha1   766aafc5e3c310bde92e405988bc7f6eb31d7cf9
    sha256 b7822c4225243215f185925724a6edff92cf18777a136cc738276c4446fac76c
  https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/org/scala-lang/scala-reflect/2.13.17/scala-reflect-2.13.17.jar
    sha1   d7ea6ad0d92e3bbe0afef1bdffbbe172704c8c47
    sha256 734533897bcfabe7a6e7fa09dbee165b257b0396e14e8a57c75111db8e04bb98
  https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/org/scala-lang/scala-compiler/2.13.17/scala-compiler-2.13.17.jar
    sha1   70f6ece2d45d2f89fb9a4d5e41181ade1bd9d416
    sha256 073ab364dc902519719bd6b9463562128abc5881d2a2e4b7a5e2d04cdd7bc025

The sha1 values are the ones Maven Central publishes next to each jar.

With sbuild, debian/make-stage0-deb downloads the jars, checks the
checksums and builds a local-only scala-2.13-stage0 .deb that installs them
to /usr/share/scala-2.13-stage0. That .deb is never uploaded:

  debian/make-stage0-deb /tmp/stage0
  sbuild --profiles=pkg.scala.stage0 \
    --extra-package=/tmp/stage0/scala-2.13-stage0_2.13.17_all.deb scala-2.13_*.dsc

Without a chroot, put the three jars in a directory and point SCALA_STAGE0
at it:

  dpkg-buildpackage -Ppkg.scala.stage0 -d SCALA_STAGE0=$HOME/scala-2.13-stage0

The stage0 build uses JDK 25 (openjdk-25-jdk-headless): the 2.13.17 STARR
cannot compile the 2.13.18 library on JDK 26 and later, where
java.util.Comparator gained default max/min methods. 2.13.18 itself handles
them (https://github.com/scala/bug/issues/13127), so normal builds use
default-jdk.

This is a NEW package, and NEW throws away the binaries of an accepted
upload (https://wiki.debian.org/ThrowAwayNewBinaries), so the bootstrap
takes three uploads: -1 stage0 source+binary to experimental, -2
source+binary to unstable, -3 source-only. From then on the archive
self-hosts and the seed is no longer used; the stage0 profile stays only to
bootstrap new architectures. A normal-profile build against the stage0
output produces byte-identical .debs.

Debian changes
--------------

 * scaladoc takes jQuery from libjs-jquery instead of a webjar
   (debian/patches/0001).
 * java-diff-utils is not packaged; -Yprint-trees:diff prints whole trees
   (debian/patches/0002).

